      "displayName": "Chris Wilper",
      "self": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/user?accountId=557058%3Ae25d94d0-bd50-4c2c-906c-14cdf85801fb",
      "timeZone": "America/Halifax"
     },
     "body": "<p>Closing as \"Wont' Fix\"...As stated before, things have changed since this was originally reported.  Mulgara is now integrated via Trippi.  It's certainly possible that it won't done that way in the future, but we should be clear on the reason/ultimate value to users.  The original idea we had for moving away from Trippi was to support direct, synchronous updates to the triplestore (via XA/JTA or a direct Mulgara/MPTStore transaction).  While Trippi is currently designed primarily around buffering of triples, but, it does now support a \"synchronous\" mode where the triples are guaranteed to have been indexed by the time the Fedora API call returns.</p>",
